
# Title:

Create and manage groups, including Security group using Azure portal

## Purpose:
Create Security group using Azure portal 

## Prerequisites:
- Microsoft 365 Business Basic (Licence)
- Group Administrator (Role)

## Procedure:

**STEP 1: OPEN AZURE ADMIN PORTAL**

1. Sign in to [Azure Portal](https://portal.azure,com)
2. On the left-hand-side top corner click on the menue button and go down to Microsoft Entra ID.

**STEP 2: CREATE GROUP**

1. Click on the Group label
2. Click on New Group to create a new group
3. Select the type on group (Security or MS365), enter the name of the group and description of the groups
4. You can assign Membership type by selecting any one of the option Assigned or Dynamic.

**STEP 3: CREATE GROUP OWNER**

1. Click on owners to  assign the owner of this group, browaer through the list and select the user.

**STEP 4: CREATE DYNAMIC MEMNERSHIP RULE**

1. If you have slected for dynamic membership, do the following step to set the Dynamic Membership Rule.
2. Under Dynamic user member click on Add dynamic query. On this page setup the expression using the property, expression and values.
3. Click on Save once you have entered the rule.


